## Troubleshooting

- **A message says the WebView2 assemblies were not found:** this Revit release
  does not ship them (Revit 2022 and 2023). Repair a 2024 or later installation, or
  see the web host section of the foundation specification for the folder a firm
  can supply.
- **A message says the browser view timed out or could not start:** the Microsoft
  Edge WebView2 Runtime is missing or blocked. Check Settings > Apps, then reopen
  the tool. Details are in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\{{ ns }}\logs\web.log`.
- **The window opens blank:** the pyRevit output panel and the log show whether
  navigation was blocked. Only `https://{{ tool_host }}/` and
  `https://{{ assets_host }}/` can be shown.
- **The button is missing:** reload the extension or restart Revit after
  confirming that the extension is installed and enabled.

